# .containerignore — prune the OCI build context for lava-api-go image builds.
#
# The lava-api-go Dockerfile uses `COPY . .` with the repo root as build
# context (docker-compose.yml `context: .`). Without this file, podman/docker
# copies the ENTIRE repo into the build container before COPY runs — including
# the multi-GB releases/ tree, .git history, and Gradle/Android build outputs.
# That filled the podman VM's layer storage and made `build_and_release.sh`
# exit 125 "no space left on device" at the COPY step (incident
# .lava-ci-evidence/sixth-law-incidents/2026-05-31-disk-pressure-podman-vm-image-build.json).
#
# The Go image build only needs the Go sources + go.mod/go.sum. Everything
# below is excluded from the build context at source — the proper fix versus
# growing the VM disk. (§6.M storage discipline; operator T7 fast-storage directive.)

# Release artifacts — gigabytes of prior + current APKs/JARs/images, never needed in the Go build.
releases/

# Version control + CI evidence
.git/
.lava-ci-evidence/

# Android / Gradle build outputs + caches
**/build/
.gradle/
app/build/
**/.cxx/
out/

# Android SDK-adjacent + local secrets (NEVER in an image — §6.H)
.env
.env.*
keystores/
app/google-services.json
local.properties

# Submodules not needed by the Go build (lava-api-go is self-contained)
submodules/
constitution/

# IDE / OS cruft
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
**/*.iml

# Node / docs export tooling
node_modules/
**/*.pdf
**/*.html
